ut then again  there's another company called orange  too so if you go to more such  correlations if you go to now Apple  orange and banana then yes you know most  likely this is talking about fruit but  you can't go and manually look at all  these such correlations and label these  documents right so instead this is  automatically done at scale it's looking  at all the triplets like Triplets of  words and asking what are the dominant  patterns that are coming out so if  they're prominently co-occurring  together maybe that's a topic that's  coming out from those core currencies  and that's what the tensile  decomposition does it's teasing out the  topics in an unsupervised way even when  you don't have labels of what the topics  are and that was the idea behind that  and that's expanding on the idea of  singular value decomposition so if  you've done like SVD you decompose the  matrix into Laura and components and now  you can expand the same to do with a  tensor as well and there's a lot of  algorithmic nuances of how to do this at  scale how you know if I have this very  large tensor I'm not going to form this  right because all I have is a vector of  frequencies for each document that is  how frequently do different words occur  in each document I don't want to form  that into a three dimensional object  because they'll be huge so I shouldn't  directly form that object but I should  implicitly manipulate that and get to  the tropics directly so there's a lot of  interesting algorithmic work to make  that happen at scale and this is  something we worked on and you know and  we showed that this is possible so so  there are also lots of advantages of  doing this tensor method as opposed to  other methods for topic modeling I won't  go into the details but there's a lot of  nice Theory you can sure that this is  guaranteed to converge to globally  optimal  solution under many natural conditions  that we expect to hold in practice and  so this was available on AWS ag