 to model and whereas we can  learn from data and then improve this  and so there's a lot of rich  possibilities of taking learning  algorithms to drones and robotics and  other control systems and I see like  tensors playing a big part there with  time series and other multi dimensional  sensors yeah so to conclude tensors are  higher dimensional extensions of  matrices and we can expand the you know  set of operations we do with matrices  two more dimensions tensor contractions  are at the core of it and we can do  operations like tensor decompositions  tensor regressions and this will expand  the class of neural networks we can use  and better capture the dimensionality is  in data as well as higher order  correlations in a low-rank form that  makes it feasible to generalize better  and also have more compact networks  thank you  you
 

